{"type":"message_update","assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"text_end","contentIndex":0,"content":"Repaired the billing migration package in `in/billingdb/`:\n\n- `migration.sql`\n  - Explicit transactional rebuild using `BEGIN IMMEDIATE`.\n  - Adds `status TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT 'open'`.\n  - Preserves invoice fields and historical timestamps.\n  - Moves orphan payments, including `p4`, to `payment_orphans`.\n  - Adds and enforces the payments-to-invoices foreign key.\n  - Supports repeat execution without duplicating orphan records or losing status values.\n  - Restores `PRAGMA foreign_keys = ON`.\n\n- `rollback.sql`\n  - Restores legacy table shapes:\n    - `invoices(id, customer_id, total_cents, created_at)`\n    - `payments(id, invoice_id, amount_cents, created_at)`\n  - Restores archived orphan payments, including `p4`.\n  - Temporarily disables foreign keys only during the transactional rebuild, then restores them.\n\n- `preflight_report.md`\n- `postcheck.sql`\n- `migration_report.md`\n\nVerification completed with Python’s SQLite engine:\n\n- First migration: 3 invoices, 3 valid payments, 1 orphan.\n- `p4` preserved with original values.\n- `PRAGMA foreign_key_check` returned no violations.\n- Invalid future payment references were rejected.\n- Second migration completed without duplication and preserved a manually changed invoice status.\n- Rollback restored legacy columns and all 4 payments, including `p4`.\n- `payment_orphans` was removed after rollback."}}
